# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# This tree is authored on Windows and built on ubuntu-latest in CI. Without this, every
# file committed from Windows lands with CRLF, and the first contributor on macOS or Linux
# produces a diff touching every line of every file they open — which buries the actual
# change and makes `git blame` useless for finding out why a number is what it is.
#
# Working copies keep whatever their platform prefers; only what git stores is normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Data files are line-normalised too — they are read by humans in diffs, and a corrected
# figure should show as one changed line.
*.json  text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
